module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.projection_drops_the_value_its_consumer_keys_on

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data projection_drops_the_value_its_consumer_keys_on: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "projection_drops_the_value_its_consumer_keys_on" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "a projection drops the authored value its consumer keys on, so every subject answers alike and a discovery gate over it greens on exactly the population it exists to find (INVALID STATE: a fact projection carries structural markers but not the authored values a downstream reader matches against; the reader returns the same answer for a declaration that names the sought thing and one that names nothing; and because the reader ANSWERS rather than refuses, the gate above it reports a clean population)",

    "WHY IT IS NOT A MISSING FEATURE BUT A FALSE NEGATIVE. The projection is not incomplete in a way anyone notices: it resolves the declaration, it returns a non-empty atom population, and every consumer downstream typechecks. What it cannot do is distinguish two declarations by what they SAY. A consumer asking 'which declarations name v1' therefore receives a confident, well-typed, empty answer, and the gate that consumes it greens. The harm is the gate's green, not the projection's gap: a lower bound is being read as a population, and the reading is invisible at every layer above the projection. ",

    "RECEIPT, measured on gunbc main at ec1571e892a rather than argued, and stated as the instrument rather than as copied numbers: test.claim.decl_fact_value_projection_witness, run over source roots dag and src/v2, reads v2.std.decl_index decl_facts_at composed with v2.std.fn_index atom_identities_in_node — the route a lexeme-keyed consumer takes. Three VALUE-ONLY pairs over purpose-built specimens in test.fixture.decl_fact_value_projection.specimens, each projecting the IDENTICAL atom population. Within every pair the two rows share declared type, shape, element count, field names and the LENGTH of every string; only the characters differ -- a bare String pair, a two-element List-of-String pair, and a record pair with one constructor and two string fields. The specimens are AUTHORED rather than borrowed for a reason this class itself supplies: an earlier revision borrowed live rows whose pairs differed in ARITY and in referenced identifiers as well as in content, so a projection that began carrying list cardinality, or a referenced declaration's atom identity, would have greened the reds while carrying no authored lexeme at all. An acceptance red whose green can be bought by something other than the named capability is not a weaker wall but a false one. ",

    "THE COMPARISON DESIGN IS THE LOAD-BEARING PART, because the first three attempts at this measurement were all defects in the instrument rather than findings: a qualified name that did not account for decl_index stripping the v2 prefix, so the lookup missed and the projection result meant nothing; a test of atom COUNT when the claim is about the LEXEME, which passes in both worlds; and a probe file moved out of the tree by a concurrent job while it was still running. The design that finally discriminates does not guess how an atom is spelled at all — it compares two populations against EACH OTHER, so 'the value is absent' cannot be confused with 'I guessed the wrong spelling'. The general rule: to test whether a projection carries a fact, vary ONLY that fact and compare outputs; never assert the presence of a value whose encoding you are inferring. ",

    "IT ALSO CORRECTED THE BRIEF THAT SENT SOMEONE TO FIX IT. The work item stated that a bare String initializer projects no atom identity WHILE A LIST-LITERAL INITIALIZER DOES, and scoped the repair to making the bare position behave like the list position. There is no such discriminator: both shapes are value-blind. Building the briefed repair would have copied a projection that also drops the value, and the discovery gate would have stayed blind while the change reported the blind spot closed — a false green on the exact axis the work existed to fix. The reading consistent with every measurement is that what surfaced for the list specimen was ExprRecordLit CONSTRUCTOR SPELLING, which v2.std.decl_facts_skeleton decl_facts_outer_record_constructor_lexeme_authority_note already records as spelling and explicitly not identity — spelling surfaces, authored values never do. A brief that names a discriminator is a measurement claim and is owed a reproduction before it is owed an implementation. ",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigation by review — nothing refuses, and the gap was found only because a consumer's green was distrusted and re-measured. ATTAINABLE CEILING: structurally guaranteed. The question 'does this declaration fact carry the authored value' is decidable and fully modelled, so once the projection carries values a lexeme-keyed reader cannot be blind to a value that is present, and the class stops depending on anyone remembering to check. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, named as the CAPABILITY and not as an artifact that would contribute to one: DataItem declaration facts carrying authored string values through decl_facts_at, sufficient for a lexeme-keyed consumer to distinguish two rows by what they author. A projection change that carries values for one initializer shape does NOT satisfy it, because a per-shape answer has the same blind spot as none — which is the error the originating brief made. ",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
